module bindings.java.hapiXmlutilXXEProtectedFactory;

// HAPI FHIR's org.hl7.fhir.utilities.xml.XMLUtil exposes a pair of factory
// constructors whose contract is the name. newXXEProtectedDocumentBuilderFactory()
// returns a DocumentBuilderFactory with disallow-doctype-decl set and XInclude
// disabled; newXXEProtectedTransformerFactory() returns a TransformerFactory
// with ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD and ACCESS_EXTERNAL_STYLESHEET set to the empty
// string. A parser or transformer built from the returned object cannot resolve
// an external entity, so the constructor call is the hardening in the same way
// a setFeature call on a local is.
//
// The JDK's own spellings are already credited at covers sameReceiver --
// setFeature with disallow-doctype-decl, setAttribute with ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD
// -- which covers a tree that hardens its own local where it builds the parser.
// HAPI centralises the features inside the constructor instead, so the call
// site carries no feature call and no receiver to key on: the factory arrives
// as the constructor's return value and the caller never re-hardens it. The
// credit has to be carried by the constructor call, and covers endpoint is the
// anchor that reaches a parser built in the same function from that value.
//
// The method segment is matched exactly and ungated. callee.method compares the
// final segment only, so the qualified XMLUtil spelling and a static import both
// match and nothing else does; both constructors are public static API on a
// class every HAPI FHIR consumer reaches through org.hl7.fhir.utilities, the
// TransformerFactory one the older of the pair and the DocumentBuilderFactory
// one its twin.
//
// This is a check and only ever suppresses. The residual is a function that
// takes one factory from the constructor and builds a second, raw one beside
// it: endpoint coverage clears both. Every function in HAPI's own tree that
// mixes the two hardens the raw factory inline, which the sameReceiver
// spellings credit on their own.

binding hapiXXEProtectedFactory {
  query pattern callExpr where callee.method in ["newXXEProtectedDocumentBuilderFactory", "newXXEProtectedTransformerFactory"]
  emit check core.XmlHardening at call {
    covers endpoint {
      anchor: call
    }
  }
}
